ven fix the basic case.\n- `SELECT '\\$name'` becomes `\"SELECT '\\\\\\\\$name'\"`. PHP prints two backslashes, then interpolates `$name` again.\n\nBackslash first works: `'\\$name'` becomes `\\\\\\$name`, which PHP prints as a literal `\\$name`. So the fix is `.replace('\\\\','\\\\\\\\').replace('\"','\\\\\"').replace('$','\\\\$')`. GHSA-3496-9g83-7v6x only covers `\\` and `\"`, so `$` isn't covered and NOT_AFFECTED isn't accurate.\n\nOn `OutputPythonFilter`: its output is a plain `'...'` literal, and Python never expands `$` there. Adding `\\$` would actually break things. Python keeps the unknown escape `\\$` as a backslash plus `$` (3.12+ also warns), so every `$` in the SQL would pick up an extra backslash. Let's leave it as is.","ttft_ms":5137,"type":"result","duration_ms":9057,"uuid":"4be6b60d-57c6-4d33-86c7-c6b6ed7ca9ad","ttft_stream_ms":1316,"time_to_request_ms":219,"first_content_frame_ms":1316,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-23T22:59:00.503Z"}

